-- Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand) -- LAYER 1: THE DEFINED TERMS (the glossary).
-- GENERATED by gen_glossary.py from the raw text: every entry's words are copied from the text by script. Edit the generator, not this file.
-- One entry for each of the 86 defined terms in the text (ss 5(1), 13, 63, 68(4), 77, 85, 94, 96(4), 121, 131(3), 141(2), 147(6), Schedule 1 clauses 2 and 6).
-- Where a definition decides something from facts, the entry says which function in which module does it; otherwise the entry is all the encoding there is.

DECLARE `How a term is defined` IS ONE OF
    `Means: a closed meaning`
    `Includes: an open list`
    `Means and includes`
    `Has the meaning set out elsewhere`

DECLARE `Defined term` HAS
    `the term` IS A STRING
    `the provision that defines it` IS A STRING
    `how the Act defines it` IS A `How a term is defined`
    `the provision named on its opening line` IS A STRING
    `the Act's words` IS A STRING
    `where this encoding decides it` IS A STRING

