GIVEN term IS A STRING
      entries IS A LIST OF `Defined term`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Defined term`
`the entries defining the term` term `among` entries MEANS
    filter (GIVEN e YIELD (e's `the term`) EQUALS term) entries

GIVEN entries IS A LIST OF `Defined term`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many entries there are in` entries MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN e YIELD 1) entries)

§ `When a definition governs`

-- The lead-ins of ss 5(1), 63, 85 and 94 each say "unless the context otherwise requires". Whether the context does is an open-textured judgment and is taken as a plain input.
-- The lead-ins of ss 13, 68(4), 77, 121, 131(3) and 147(6) and of Schedule 1 clause 2 only fix where a definition applies ("in legislation", "in this section", "in this Part"):
-- that scope is the field `the provision that defines it` of each entry.
-- src:46 | In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires,—
-- src:425 | In sections 64 to 66 and Schedule 2, unless the context otherwise requires,—
-- src:626 | In this subpart, unless the context otherwise requires,—
-- src:701 | In this subpart, unless the context otherwise requires,—
@ref Legislation Act 2019 ss 5(1), 63, 85 and 94, lead-ins (src:46) (src:425) (src:626) (src:701)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a definition in the Act governs the use of the term` `the context otherwise requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the context otherwise requires`)

